.TH MITOS-UTILS-COMPAT 7 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS Miscellany"
.SH NAME
mitos\-utils\-compat \- POSIX/GNU compatibility scope of mitos\-utils
.SH DESCRIPTION
mitos\-utils implements the commonly\-used subset of POSIX/GNU
coreutils behavior for each of its ~50 utilities, not full
flag\-for\-flag parity. This page is a pointer, not the full
reference: see
.I docs/compatibility.md
in the mitos\-utils source tree for the complete per\-utility table of
what's supported and what's deliberately out of scope, and
.I docs/architecture.md
for why the project is organized this way.
.SH THE SHORT VERSION
.TP
.B Binary safety
The text utilities operate on UTF\-8 text line\-by\-line, not raw
bytes; they are not binary\-safe the way GNU's versions are.
.TP
.B Locale
C\-locale behavior only (byte\-order comparisons); no LC_COLLATE\-aware
sorting or multi\-byte\-aware character counting.
.TP
.B Platform scope
.BR chmod (1),
.BR chown (1),
.BR chgrp (1),
.BR mount (1),
.BR umount (1),
.BR sync (1),
.BR dmesg (1),
and
.BR kill (1)
are unix\-only by construction.
.BR ps (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR uptime (1),
and
.BR dmesg (1)
additionally require Linux specifically (they read
.IR /proc ).
.TP
.B FFI verification
Hand\-written libc bindings for
.BR statvfs (3),
.BR mount (2),
and
.BR syslog (2)
have been cross\-checked against current man pages; see
.I docs/compatibility.md
for exactly what has and hasn't been verified this way.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-security (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
